---
import ShineText from "@/components/shine-text/ShineText.astro";
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const lastUpdated = "August 25, 2026";
const contactEmail = "contact@goldsimulations.com";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="What Gold Simulations collects, why, who processes it, and how to have it deleted."
  navStyle="default"
>
  <section class="site-container pt-24 pb-8 md:pt-28">
    <div class="max-w-3xl">
      <h1 class="h1"><ShineText>Privacy</ShineText> Policy</h1>
      <p class="description mt-4">Last updated {lastUpdated}.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="site-container markdown-content max-w-3xl pb-20 md:pb-24">
    <p>
      Gold Simulations builds economics simulation games for classrooms. This policy covers
      <strong>goldsimulations.com</strong> and the newsletter you can subscribe to from it. It is written
      to be read, not to protect us — if anything here is unclear, email
      <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a> and we will explain it.
    </p>

    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>The only thing this website collects from you is <strong>your email address</strong>, and only if you type it into the subscribe form.</li>
      <li>We <strong>have never sold personal information and never will</strong>, to anyone, for any price.</li>
      <li>There are <strong>no analytics, no advertising trackers, and no third-party scripts</strong> on this site.</li>
      <li>You can leave at any time using the unsubscribe link in any email, or by emailing us.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>

    <h3>Your email address</h3>
    <p>
      When you subscribe, we store the address you entered, the date you subscribed, and whether you have
      confirmed it. We use double opt-in: after you submit the form we email you a confirmation link, and
      you are not added to the list until you click it. This protects you from being signed up by someone
      else.
    </p>
    <p>
      We do not ask for your name, your institution, or anything else. If you email us directly, we will
      have whatever you chose to put in that email.
    </p>

    <h3>Standard server logs</h3>
    <p>
      Our hosting provider records ordinary web server logs — IP address, browser user agent, the page
      requested, and a timestamp — as an automatic part of serving the site. These are used for security
      and troubleshooting. We do not combine them with your email address or use them to build a profile.
    </p>

    <h3>What we do not collect</h3>
    <p>
      No analytics platform, advertising pixel, session recorder, or social media tracker runs on this
      site. Our fonts are served from our own domain rather than a font provider, so simply reading these
      pages does not report your visit to any third party.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p>
      This site sets <strong>no tracking cookies</strong>. Because there is nothing to consent to, you will
      not see a cookie banner. If we ever add analytics, we will add a genuine consent control and update
      this policy before turning it on — not after.
    </p>

    <h2>Who processes your data</h2>
    <p>
      We keep your information in three services, each of which acts as a processor on our behalf under
      contract. We do not hand your data to anyone else.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Supabase</strong> — the database holding the subscriber list.</li>
      <li><strong>Resend</strong> — sends the confirmation email and the newsletter, and holds the mailing list used to send it.</li>
      <li><strong>Netlify</strong> — hosts the website and produces the server logs described above.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      These providers store data on servers in the United States. If you are subscribing from outside the
      US, your email address will be transferred there.
    </p>

    <h2>Email tracking</h2>
    <p>
      Open tracking and click tracking are <strong>switched off</strong> on our sending domain. We do not
      embed tracking pixels in our emails, and we do not know whether you opened one or which links you
      followed. We can see delivery-level information from our email provider — whether a message was
      accepted, bounced, or reported as spam — which is necessary to keep the list healthy.
    </p>

    <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>
      We keep your email address until you unsubscribe or ask us to delete it. When you unsubscribe we
      retain a record that the address opted out, so that we do not accidentally email you again. Server
      logs are kept for a short period by our host and then rotated out.
    </p>

    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Unsubscribe</strong> — every email includes an unsubscribe link, which takes effect immediately.</li>
      <li><strong>Ask what we hold</strong> — email us and we will tell you exactly what is stored against your address.</li>
      <li><strong>Correction or deletion</strong> — email us and we will correct or erase your record.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Depending on where you live you may have additional rights under laws such as the GDPR or the CCPA,
      including the right to a copy of your data, to object to processing, or to complain to a supervisory
      authority. We honour these requests regardless of where you live. Our lawful basis for sending the
      newsletter is your consent, which you gave by confirming your subscription and can withdraw at any
      time.
    </p>
    <p>
      Send any request to <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>. We aim to respond within
      a few days and will not charge you for it.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      Our products are sold to educators and institutions, and this newsletter is intended for teachers,
      instructors, and administrators. It is not directed at children, and we do not knowingly collect
      information from anyone under 16 through this website. If you believe a child has subscribed, email
      us and we will remove the address.
    </p>
    <p>
      EconRunes is not yet available. When student accounts launch, the handling of student data will be
      governed by a separate agreement with each school or institution, and this policy will be updated to
      describe it.
    </p>

    <h2>Security</h2>
    <p>
      The subscriber list is stored with row-level security enabled and is reachable only by our server
      using a privileged key that is never exposed to your browser. The site is served over HTTPS
      throughout.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      If we change how we handle your information we will update this page and change the date at the top.
      For a material change affecting existing subscribers — a new processor, a new purpose — we will say
      so in the newsletter rather than quietly editing this page.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Gold Simulations — <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
